Material Selection Influences Optical Performance

Material characteristics are important in determining the performance and manufacturing suitability of light guide plates.

The report covers PMMA and polycarbonate/other optical polymers.

PMMA is particularly relevant because of its optical transparency and suitability for light transmission applications. Other optical polymers provide additional material options according to product and manufacturing requirements.

Precision Manufacturing Is Shaping Product Development

Manufacturing processes influence the optical characteristics and dimensional consistency of light guide plates.

The report identifies printing, laser/engraving and injection molding/other manufacturing methods.

Thinner plates, higher optical efficiency and precision micro-patterning are important technology directions influencing new product development.

These developments are particularly relevant as display manufacturers seek to improve optical performance while reducing product thickness.

Asia-Pacific Leads the LGP Market

